---
/**
 * The second of Rahul's two output panels. It starts where
 * `TaxIncomeComputation` stops — at total income, already split into the part
 * the slabs work on and the part taxed at its own rates — and carries it down
 * to the figure the reader owes.
 *
 * Design settled before the component in `TaxComputation.checks.md`.
 *
 * It states the working, not the verdict: `TaxAnswer` is rung 1 and says which
 * regime is cheaper in a sentence. What emphasis appears here is applied by the
 * page's one `verdictFor()`, never by a class written in this file — that is
 * the whole of sol-043, which is why `taxColNew` / `taxColOld` and the two
 * total cells are handles rather than styled markup.
 */
---

<section
  id="taxComputation"
  class="rounded-2xl border border-navy-200 dark:border-white/10 bg-white dark:bg-navy-900/40 p-5 sm:p-6 space-y-4"
  aria-label="How your taxable income becomes a bill"
>
  <div class="space-y-1">
    <h3 class="text-base font-bold text-navy-900 dark:text-navy-100">Tax computation</h3>
    <p class="text-sm text-navy-600 dark:text-navy-400 leading-relaxed">
      What the slabs charge, what the rebate gives back, and what is added on top.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="overflow-x-auto">
    <table class="w-full text-left text-sm">
      <thead>
        <tr class="border-b border-navy-200 dark:border-navy-800 text-navy-600 dark:text-navy-400">
          <th class="py-2 font-semibold">Item</th>
          <th id="taxColNew" class="py-2 text-right font-semibold w-28">New regime</th>
          <th id="taxColOld" class="py-2 text-right font-semibold w-28">Old regime</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody
        id="taxRows"
        class="divide-y divide-navy-200 dark:divide-navy-800 text-navy-900 dark:text-navy-100"
      ></tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <!--
    Marginal relief is the one line whose name explains nothing, so it carries a
    sentence — and the sentence states the principle rather than the reader's
    position, so it stays true at every input (dd-008). It is written only when
    the relief actually bit.
  -->
  <p id="taxMarginalNote" class="text-sm text-navy-600 dark:text-navy-400 leading-relaxed empty:hidden"></p>

  <!--
    The slab working. The engine has always returned it and the page has never
    shown it: it is the answer to the reader who asks which slab their last
    rupee fell in, and genuinely optional to everyone else, which is exactly
    what a disclosure is for.
  -->
  <details class="tax-chip rounded-xl border border-navy-200 dark:border-navy-800 bg-navy-50 dark:bg-navy-900/60 px-4 py-3">
    <summary class="text-sm font-semibold text-navy-900 dark:text-navy-100">Which slab each rupee fell in</summary>
    <div class="pt-4 space-y-4">
      <p class="text-sm text-navy-600 dark:text-navy-400 leading-relaxed">
        The two regimes draw their bands in different places, so they are shown as two ladders
        rather than one table pretending the bands line up. Only gains taxed at their own rates sit
        outside both.
      </p>
      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-4">
        <div class="space-y-2">
          <h4 class="text-sm font-semibold text-navy-900 dark:text-navy-100">New regime</h4>
          <table class="w-full text-left text-sm">
            <tbody
              id="slabRowsNew"
              class="divide-y divide-navy-200 dark:divide-navy-800 text-navy-900 dark:text-navy-100"
            ></tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
        <div class="space-y-2">
          <h4 class="text-sm font-semibold text-navy-900 dark:text-navy-100">Old regime</h4>
          <table class="w-full text-left text-sm">
            <tbody
              id="slabRowsOld"
              class="divide-y divide-navy-200 dark:divide-navy-800 text-navy-900 dark:text-navy-100"
            ></tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </details>
</section>

<style>
  .tax-chip > summary {
    cursor: pointer;
    list-style: none;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 0.5rem;
  }
  .tax-chip > summary::-webkit-details-marker {
    display: none;
  }
  .tax-chip > summary::after {
    content: '+';
    font-weight: 400;
    font-size: 1rem;
    line-height: 1;
    opacity: 0.5;
  }
  .tax-chip[open] > summary::after {
    content: '\2212';
  }
</style>
